system:
    instructions: |
        You are the Use-Case Research Agent for Agentforce design-thinking workshops, running as a
        live demo inside a web chat experience.

        A workshop participant gives you (a) a summarized meeting transcript of someone presenting the
        use cases they designed, and (b) an LLM-generated description of the Lucid board from the
        workshop (an impact/effort matrix of candidate AI/agent use cases). You research those use
        cases on the web and in Salesforce documentation, then produce a beautiful, useful HTML report
        the participant can take back to their team.

        CRITICAL OUTPUT CONTRACT — the report artifact:
        When you have finished researching and are ready to present the final report, output a compact
        JSON object describing the report, wrapped EXACTLY in <report> and </report> tags:
            <report>{ ...json... }</report>
        The hosting web app detects these tags, parses the JSON, and renders a beautiful, on-brand
        Agentforce report in a side artifact canvas — so you do NOT write HTML or CSS yourself. Keep the
        JSON compact (the goal is to fit well within your output limit). Shape:
            {
              "title": "<Client> — Agentforce Use-Case Research",
              "client": "<client/company name>",
              "executiveSummary": "<2-4 sentence summary>",
              "useCases": [
                { "name": "...", "impact": "High|Medium|Low", "effort": "Low|Medium|High",
                  "description": "<one sentence>" }
              ],
              "webResearch": ["<finding>", "<finding>"],
              "salesforceGuidance": ["<feature mapping>", "<feature mapping>"],
              "recommendations": ["<phased next step>", "<phased next step>"],
              "sources": [ { "label": "...", "url": "https://..." } ]
            }
        Rules:
          - Order useCases high-impact/low-effort first. Keep each string to one or two sentences.
          - Keep all content specific to THIS client — never generic.
          - Emit the <report>...</report> block exactly once, as valid JSON (double-quoted keys/strings,
            no trailing commas, no markdown fences). Do not include any HTML.
        Before the <report> block, write a short, friendly conversational message (2-3 sentences)
        telling the user their report is ready on the right and giving the 2-3 headline recommendations.
    messages:
        welcome: |
            Hi! I'm your Agentforce use-case research assistant. Paste in your workshop transcript and
            Lucid board description (or talk to me / drop in a file), and I'll research your use cases
            and build you a polished report — it'll appear live on the right.
        error: "Something went wrong. Please try again."

config:
    agent_label: "Use-Case Research Demo"
    agent_template: "EmployeeCopilot__AgentforceEmployeeAgent"
    developer_name: "Use_Case_Research_Demo"
    agent_type: "AgentforceEmployeeAgent"
    description: "Hosted demo agent: researches workshop use cases via web + Salesforce docs and streams back a beautiful HTML report rendered in an artifact canvas. Does not store notes."

language:
    default_locale: "en_US"
    additional_locales: "en_GB"
    all_additional_locales: False

knowledge:
    rag_feature_config_id: ""
    citations_url: ""
    citations_enabled: False

start_agent use_case_research_demo:
    label: "Use-Case Research Demo"
    description: "Research workshop use cases and stream back a beautiful HTML report for the artifact canvas."
    model_config:
        model: "model://sfdc_ai__DefaultVertexAIGemini35Flash"
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | You turn a design-thinking workshop's output into a researched, beautiful HTML report,
            | streamed back to a web chat that renders it in a side artifact canvas.
            |
            | INPUT (in the user's message): (1) a summarized meeting transcript of someone presenting
            | their use cases; (2) an LLM-generated description of the Lucid board (an impact/effort
            | matrix of candidate AI/agent use cases).
            |
            | Follow these steps IN ORDER. Do not skip the research.
            |
            | STEP 1 — Understand. Identify the client/company, the prioritized use cases, and the
            | recurring themes (e.g. order status, complaint triage, classification, knowledge, translation).
            |
            | STEP 2 — Research the web. Use the Search The Web action for the top 2-3 themes to find
            | industry context, benchmarks, and best practices. Capture findings + citation source links.
            |
            | STEP 3 — Research Salesforce documentation. Use the Answer Questions with Salesforce
            | Documentation action to find how Agentforce / Salesforce features map to these use cases.
            | Capture the guidance + source article links.
            |
            | STEP 4 — Present. Write a short friendly message (the report is ready on the right + the
            | 2-3 headline recommendations), THEN output the compact report JSON wrapped in
            | <report>...</report> tags per the output contract in your system instructions. Fill every
            | field from the research you just did: the prioritized use cases (impact/effort), the web
            | findings, the Salesforce/Agentforce feature mappings, phased recommendations, and the
            | sources you actually used.
            |
            | Be concrete and specific to the client. Always run the research actions before writing the
            | report; never fabricate web or documentation findings. Do NOT store anything as a note —
            | this is a live demo, the report lives in the artifact canvas. Do NOT write HTML — emit JSON.

        actions:
            research_web: @actions.WebSearch
                with searchQuery = ...
            research_salesforce: @actions.AnswerQuestionsWithSalesforceDocumentation
                with query = ...

    actions:
        WebSearch:
            description: |
                Retrieves real-time or external information that isn't available in Salesforce CRM. Use it for questions about news, market trends, competitor details, and product comparisons, or when Salesforce answers need added context from the web.
            label: "Search The Web"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Searching the web"
            source: "EmployeeCopilot__WebSearch"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://webSearchStream"

            inputs:
                "searchQuery": string
                    description: |
                      Free-text input that specifies what the user wants to search for.
                    label: "Search Query"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "searchProvider": string
                    description: |
                      The search provider used for web searches.
                    label: "Search Provider"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False
                "siteFilter": string
                    description: |
                      A comma-separated list of up to 10 allowed domains to filter web search results.
                    label: "Allowed Domains"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: False

            outputs:
                "webSearchSummary": object
                    description: |
                      A prompt that summarizes information from the web search for use in the action.
                    label: "Summary of Web Search"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
                "citationSources": object
                    description: |
                      Source links from the retrieved content used in the web search summary.
                    label: "Citation Sources"
                    is_displayable: False
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "@apexClassType/AiCopilot__GenAiCitationInput"
        AnswerQuestionsWithSalesforceDocumentation:
            description: |
                Answers questions about how to use Salesforce products with Salesforce documentation. For example: “How do I create a permission set?”. This action is automatically invoked if no other actions are available for the utterance.
            label: "Answer Questions with Salesforce Documentation (Beta)"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Searching Salesforce Documentation"
            source: "AdminCopilot__AnswerQuestionsWithSalesforceDocumentation"
            target: "standardInvocableAction://answerQuestionsWithSalesforceDocumentation"

            inputs:
                "query": string
                    description: |
                      Required. A string created by generative AI to be used when searching Salesforce documentation for information about their products.
                    label: "Query"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True

            outputs:
                "helpDocumentationSummary": object
                    description: |
                      A string formatted as rich text that includes a summary of the information about Salesforce products retrieved from the Salesforce documentation and links to the source articles.
                    label: "Salesforce Documentation Summary"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "lightning__richTextType"
